    <note type="project" target="#dat1">Whitman probably wrote this manuscript draft not long before submitting it for publication to the <hi rend="italic">Herald</hi>, with which he was under contract to produce ten poems each month (see <hi rend="italic">With Walt Whitman in Camden</hi> [Boston: Small, Maynard &amp; Company, 1906] <ref target="med.00001.019">1:41&#8211;42</ref>).</note>
     <note type="work_relations" target="xxx.00327" cert="high">
      <p>"To-day and Thee" was first published in the 23 April 1888 issue of the <hi rend="italic">New York Herald</hi>. With corrections and minor revisions, it was later included in <hi rend="italic">November Boughs</hi> (1888).</p>
     </note>
